### New committed rows in `noBrowserPricing.test.ts` (names say the behaviour; each expected value hand-written; the existing six untouched in name and expectation; the helper `scan` may change its body to call the new API but not its meaning)
- One row per plant, built from an IN-MEMORY file set given to the same Program machinery (a virtual host: the plant text plus the minimal `schema.ts`/`format` stand-ins it needs), each asserting a finding with the hand-written kind and line; and a GREEN twin per form (the same shape on a COUNT name, on a formatted value, on a non-money string) asserting `[]`. If the virtual host cannot resolve the real `schema.ts`, the row builds a two-file miniature that declares one `["Decimal"]` member: say so.
